/-!
# Actual complex-level specialization models

This package constructs the literal frozen and varying-twist nonzero
fibres from the original free phase-plane quotient.  The compact base
phase is retained, and the independently prescribed collapse is proved
to be the corresponding compensated central rotation.  Genuine homotopies
give the all-degree integral singular homology comparison with the
original marked product collapse.  Every nonzero complex level is covered,
and the required small radius is derived from holomorphic period data.

This comparison does not assert any unproved matrix formula or homological
surjectivity of the product collapse; those are separate geometric results.
-/
